        "Paced breathing means you stop breathing at whatever rate your body picks and breathe at one you chose. The rate is slower than usual, and it stays the same from one breath to the next. The versions differ only in the numbers.",
        "Most guides land in the same place. A menopause resource, My Menoplan, gives 4 in and 6 out. Now Matters Now, which teaches skills from dialectical behaviour therapy (DBT), suggests 5 seconds in and 7 out, or any pace that suits you as long as the exhale is longer than the inhale. Oxygen Advantage starts people at 3 in and 5 out through the nose, then 4 in and 6 out.",
