      h2: 'Turning breaths per minute into seconds',
      paras: [
        "Instructions mix breaths per minute and seconds per phase, and the two are easy to confuse. The conversion is one division: 60 divided by the length of one full breath in seconds gives breaths per minute.",
        "So 4 seconds in and 6 out is a 10-second breath, which is 6 breaths a minute. My Menoplan's page gives that same 4 and 6 count and then calls the goal 10 breaths a minute. If the counts are seconds, the two can't both be right. Ten breaths a minute is a 6-second breath, say 2.5 in and 3.5 out. Decide which number you're following before you start.",
      ],
